WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:06.410
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, amen.

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:14.330
The reading from the Sinaxarion, for September 28, on which we commemorate, our righteous

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:19.680
Father, Carito, the Confessor.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:26.720
On the 28th of the month, we celebrate the memory of our venerable Father, Carito, Confessor

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:31.300
and Teacher of the Desert.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:38.280
Our Holy Father, Carito, was born and brought up at Econium in Asia Minor.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:46.860
The Emperor, Aurelion, in the years 270 through 276, who showed no hostility to Christians

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:54.700
at the outset of his reign, was incited by the devil after a while to begin a violent persecution

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:59.020
of those who called upon the name of Christ.

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:05.940
Carito, whose piety and godliness were well-known in Econium, was arrested and brought before

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:10.980
the consul when the imperial decree arrived.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:19.180
As he fearlessly confessed Christ and his abhorrence of idols, he was stretched on the ground,

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:26.780
violently scourged and thrown into prison with his flesh, torn to shreds.

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:34.700
A few days later, after a second appearance at the tribunal, he was set free and took refuge

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:42.740
in Egypt until the death of the tyrant put an end to persecution for a time.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:49.060
Having in his body the marks of the Passion of Christ Saint Carito achieved his martyrdom

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:58.860
by ever-grader zeal with which he followed the Lord in a life of Askees and renunciation.

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:05.060
Unlooked for trials came his way besides those voluntary afflictions by which he subdued

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:12.300
his body and made its subject and obedient to the Law of the Spirit.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:17.500
One day he fell among thieves as he was going up to Jerusalem.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:25.060
They bound him hand and foot and took him to their cave at a place called Faran, where God

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:32.140
soon executed his judgment upon them, for they drank wine polluted by snake venom and

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:33.780
died.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:39.940
Carito was miraculously freed from his bonds and found himself in possession of the booty

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:42.460
amassed by the brigands.

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:49.660
He distributed part of these ill-gotten goods to the poor and part he used to build churches

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:52.100
to the glory of God.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:59.180
He then settled in the cave himself and lived there in Askees.

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:05.940
While dwelling at Faran, Saint Carito brought many infidels to embrace the faith and to follow

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:09.020
the example of his angelic life.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:12.920
But he wanted to find again his beloved solitude.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:18.940
He therefore placed the best of his disciples at the head of the community and exhorted

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:25.700
his spiritual children to observe a strict temperance in food and sleep.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:33.500
To pray day and night at the hours he had appointed them and to receive the poor and strangers

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:36.300
as Christ himself.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:41.620
He then settled in a cave on Mount Dukas near Jericho.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:47.420
However, he was not left to converse alone with God.

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:54.740
Many disciples came to join him and he had to establish a second laura before fleeing

00:03:54.740 --> 00:04:00.580
once again to a place more remote called the Kuh.

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:08.640
He later settled with a few disciples in a third laura called in Syriac, Suka, or

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:10.980
the old laura.

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:17.040
But nothing could stop the flow of his new disciples and of pagans who came to taste the

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:24.940
honey of his words and to look upon this living image of Christ.

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:31.220
Askariton sought nothing but the sweetness of union with God in solitude.

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:38.220
He withdrew to a cave above the laura that could be reached only by using ladders.

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:43.780
He dwelt there for many years, taking water from a spring that flowed in the cave at his

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:45.980
prayer.

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:53.220
Knowing beforehand the date of his death, he was brought back to his first laura of Faran,

00:04:53.220 --> 00:05:00.340
where as a spiritual testament, he gave his disciples to understand that Askisis linked

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:08.660
with humility and love towards all without exception is the sure way to arrive at union

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:10.860
with God.

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:20.460
His last word spoken, St. Kariton lay on his bed and fell asleep in peace to take his place

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:25.260
in the choir of angels and saints.

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:31.940
Through the prayers of our holy fathers, O Lord, Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:33.060
and save us.
